# Bare service-page paths (/photography -> /photography.html) are
# intentionally NOT redirected here: @astrojs/cloudflare's own
# matchStaticAsset()/fallbackToAssets() strip ".html" internally and fetch
# the bare path from the assets binding to resolve prerendered pages (see
# wrangler.jsonc's comment). An explicit redirect rule for the exact same
# bare path creates a redirect loop with that internal resolution. The
# platform's default html_handling ("auto-trailing-slash") already serves
# /photography.html's content directly at /photography with no redirect
# needed, and the canonical <link> tag (SEO.astro) points at the *.html
# URL regardless of which form was requested.

# Bot traps (wp-admin, .env, .git, phpmyadmin, etc.) are intentionally not
# listed here: Cloudflare Workers Assets' _redirects only allows 200/301/
# 302/303/307/308, not 404 — and these paths don't exist as real files
# anyway, so they already 404 through the site's normal 404.html without
# needing an explicit rule.
/.well-known/security.txt /security.txt 200

# Short addresses for the legal pages.
/impressum /legal/impressum.html 301
/datenschutz /legal/datenschutz.html 301

